menu "ThistleOS debug"
    config THISTLE_TAILNET_CHAT_SPIKE
        bool "Tailnet chat spike: a WebSocket echo on the tailnet, and an Opus bench"
        default n
        depends on IDF_TARGET_ESP32S3
        help
            Ticket 01 of Tailnet chat (.scratch/tailnet-chat/issues/). While
            the tailnet is connected, echoes WebSocket frames on TCP port
            4810 of the device's tailnet address, refusing any connection
            not from the tailnet, logs the lwIP sockets open, and once times
            Opus at 16 kHz mono on a task of its own. It holds the device
            awake. Throwaway: leave it off.
endmenu
